Package: proxmod-example-hello
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${perl:Depends},
 proxmod (>= 0.2.0),
Description: reference proxmod extension for Proxmox VE
 A complete, minimal proxmod extension: one REST endpoint tree under
 /nodes/{node}/proxmod/example-hello and one tab in the node view of the
 Proxmox VE web interface.
 .
 It exists to be read. It is the smallest package that exercises the whole
 extension contract, and it has no maintainer scripts of any kind: it ships a
 Perl module, a manifest and a JavaScript file, and proxmod's dpkg trigger does
 the rest. Installing and removing it leaves every Proxmox-owned file byte for
 byte unchanged.
